rl":"https://api.github.com/users/IchirokuXVI/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/IchirokuXVI","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IchirokuXVI/nx-portfolio/commits/8a9a87dc5b84a8bb65b3bf8fd9ab98756e49ad5e/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-07T13:30:30Z","email":"danieliyo65@gmail.com","name":"Ichiroku"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-07T13:30:30Z","email":"danieliyo65@gmail.com","name":"Ichiroku"},"message":"fix(luna-shopper-admin): the places queue after its review (plan 0061)\n\nThe other chain question names its shop and goes when another shop or\nchain is on screen, so \"Link anyway\" sends only the shop it names. The\npreview of the bulk act is dropped by a decision and by a reload, and the\nnotice counts what the second read linked beyond it. A decision and the\nbulk act lock each other, and a second press sends nothing.\n\nA refused import whose reference another shop holds (backend plan 0195)\nnames the holder and offers the link and no new shop. A link says when\nthe reference was left empty. A link of a place decided elsewhere says so\nand takes the row out. A shop with no label and no address is never\ncalled by its id.\n\nThe memory harvester follows the gateway on the 50 m bound, the chain\nname, the chain of an import, the floor area, the provider and the taken\nreference.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"8f7e5372cf94cd5498fbb386c7f94ee9d37aba49","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IchirokuXVI/nx-portfolio/git/trees/8f7e5372cf94cd5498fbb386c7f94ee9d37aba49"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IchirokuXVI/nx-portfolio/git/commits/8a9a87dc5b84a8bb65b3bf8fd9ab98756e49ad5e","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/63235844?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/IchirokuXVI