l":"https://api.github.com/users/IchirokuXVI/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/IchirokuXVI/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/IchirokuXVI/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/IchirokuXVI/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/IchirokuXVI","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IchirokuXVI/nx-portfolio/commits/632664a06bd10be7e3436a7d465ff9ab6751ca9a/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-07T12:43:08Z","email":"danieliyo65@gmail.com","name":"Ichiroku"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-07T12:43:08Z","email":"danieliyo65@gmail.com","name":"Ichiroku"},"message":"fix(luna): a shop reference that is taken answers its own refusal (plan 0194)\n\nCatalog holds one shop for each external reference\n(uq_locations_external_ref, on the reference alone). A write that gave a\nshop a reference another shop holds reached the index, and the gateway\nanswered 500.\n\nCatalog now answers 409 location_external_ref_taken with the holder in\ndetails.heldBy, checked before the write and also made from the refusal\nof the index, so a race answers the same code. A link of a place leaves\nthe reference empty, links, and names the holder in refHeldBy. An import\npasses the refusal through, and force creates the shop with no reference.\nA trusted run logs the reason and goes on.\n\nNo migration: the manifest counts do not move. The index on provider and\nreference is written in the plan as a follow up.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"c8be2e33cf8f989e12c0a99fdc602e9461b5925e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IchirokuXVI/nx-portfolio/git/trees/c8be2e33cf8f989e12c0a99fdc602e9461b5925e"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IchirokuXVI/nx-portfolio/git/commits/632664a06bd10be7e3436a7d465ff9ab6751ca9a","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null